  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "A thousand American soldiers fought the war with inflatable tanks. The 23rd Headquarters Special Troops. Activated January 1944. Their job was to be seen.",
        "visual_query": "wwii european battlefield france 1944",
        "visual_fallback": "wartime army camp"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Rubber tanks, rubber jeeps, rubber artillery. Crews could raise a whole armoured division in a few hours, then pack it into trucks by morning.",
        "visual_query": "military trucks muddy french road",
        "visual_fallback": "army truck convoy"
      },
      {
        "narration": "How do you fake an army after dark? With sound. Engine noise taped at Fort Knox, blasted from halftrack speakers, audible fifteen miles away.",
        "visual_query": "german forest winter front 1944",
        "visual_fallback": "dark forest night"
      },
      {
        "narration": "They ran more than twenty of these shows across France, Luxembourg and Germany, pulling enemy fire toward empty fields while real divisions moved elsewhere.",
        "visual_query": "luxembourg countryside empty winter field",
        "visual_fallback": "empty rural field"
      },
      {
        "narration": "And nobody could be told. The files stayed classified until 1996, and the surviving men only got their Congressional Gold Medal in March 2024.",
        "visual_query": "united states capitol washington exterior",
        "visual_fallback": "old army archive"
      }
    ],
